    "author": "AUD-07 slice 1 (Claude)",
    "notes": "AUD-07 C13c: max_pos=1; SOL (first in slot order) and XRP both arm on the close of 279. SOL arms first and holds the only slot, so XRP is blocked at arming (slot check = len(open) + len(armed) + len(resting) >= max_pos). XRP rebounds 2 % in candle 280 but has no armed entry. SOL falls to 99 in the red candle 280 (no rebound), then rebounds 0.5 ATR to 99.5 in 281 (the leg end): it fills at 99.5 x 1.0002 = 99.5199, qty 10/30, and exits on the signal of 290 at 99.5 x 0.9998. R = (-0.0398 - 199 x 0.0005) / 30 = -0.0046433. Redesigned after the Codex review on 4e03152 (P1-3): the old expectation (no trades) also passed when both signals were ignored."
